      "writtenOn": "2024-01-05T19:25:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the sensors lose power in S3, make sure their `active-mask` is `SENSOR_ACTIVE_S0`, not `ACTIVE_S0_S3`.",
      "revId": "d078f6cd5331047d81d3b5fd93822d476fc26561",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a347f3c4_da391070",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1182824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-05T21:37:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The sensor is actually binding to S3 rails on Corsola. However, the rail is from AP PMIC. When AP issues a shutdown command, the PMIC would turn it off immediately in S0, and then EC is aware of the S0-\u003eS3 transition later. This would cause the i2c communication to fail while setting the data rate to 0 in S0-\u003eS3 transition. \n\nDo you have any other suggestion for this one?",
      "parentUuid": "dc942192_b76926a2",
      "revId": "d078f6cd5331047d81d3b5fd93822d476fc26561",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f481156d_a05efd4e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1182824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-05T21:41:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "... and in suspend, this won\u0027t happen since the PMIC and sensor are still powered on, and we can safely  set the sampling rate to 0.",
      "parentUuid": "a347f3c4_da391070",
      "revId": "d078f6cd5331047d81d3b5fd93822d476fc26561",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
